k_dynasty_(Delhi)","c":3},{"y":1227,"t":"gain","x":"1227: Mandore.","cp":"unnamed ruler of Mandore","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":3},{"y":1228,"t":"contest_end","x":"4 May 1228: Uch falls after a three-month siege; Qabacha drowns himself in the Indus on 26 May.","m":5,"cp":"Qabacha of Multan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":3},{"y":1228,"t":"gain","x":"1228: Multan and Uch.","m":5,"cp":"Qabacha of Multan","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":3},{"y":1229,"t":"vassal_start","x":"18 February 1229: the caliph's deed of investiture reaches Delhi.","m":2,"cp":"abbasid-caliphate","cpn":"Abbasid Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":2},{"y":1232,"t":"gain","x":"12 December 1232: Gwalior.","m":12,"cp":"rulers of Gwalior","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":3},{"y":1233,"t":"contest_start","x":"c. 1233: Kalinjar attacked. Under Malik Nusratuddin Taisi 'Kalinjar was attacked and plundered for about 50 days, around 1233-34'.","cp":"chandela-kingdom","cpn":"Chandela kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":2},{"y":1234,"t":"contest_end","x":"c. 1234: the Kalinjar raid ends without annexation.","cp":"chandela-kingdom","cpn":"Chandela kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":2},{"y":1234,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1234-35: Iltutmish's army occupies Bhilsa.","cp":"paramara-dynasty","cpn":"Paramara dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":2},{"y":1234,"t":"contest_start","x":"1234: Iltutmish raids Ujjain.","cp":"paramara-dynasty","cpn":"Paramara dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":3},{"y":1235,"t":"contest_end","x":"1235: the Ujjain raid ends; no land is annexed ('made little effort to annex the Paramara territory').","cp":"paramara-dynasty","cpn":"Paramara dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":3},{"y":1239,"t":"occupation_end","x":"By 1239 (bridge): Devapala regains Bhilsa.","cp":"paramara-dynasty","cpn":"Paramara dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":1},{"y":1241,"t":"contest_start","x":"30 December 1241: the Mongols sack Lahore.","m":12,"cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_India","c":3},{"y":1243,"t":"contest_start","x":"1243: the Odia army moves on Bengal.","cp":"eastern-ganga-kingdom","cpn":"Eastern Ganga Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narasingha_Deva_I","c":2},{"y":1244,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1244: Odia forces occupy Rarh and Gauda of Mamluk Bengal.","cp":"eastern-ganga-kingdom","cpn":"Eastern Ganga Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narasingha_Deva_I","c":2},{"y":1247,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1247 (bridge): the occupation of Rarh and Gauda is taken to end.","cp":"eastern-ganga-kingdom","cpn":"Eastern Ganga Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narasingha_Deva_I","c":1},{"y":1247,"t":"contest_end","x":"1247: Yuzbak is appointed governor of Bengal 'to free Bengal from Odia forces'; Paramardi Dev was killed in the fighting.","cp":"eastern-ganga-kingdom","cpn":"Eastern Ganga Kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narasingha_Deva_I","c":1},{"y":1247,"t":"contest_start","x":"1247: Balban puts down a rising in Kalinjar.","cp":"chandela-kingdom","cpn":"Chandela kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban","c":3},{"y":1247,"t":"contest_end","x":"1247: the Kalinjar rising is suppressed.","cp":"chandela-kingdom","cpn":"Chandela kingdom","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban","c":3},{"y":1258,"t":"vassal_end","x":"February 1258 (bridge): the allegiance ends with the caliphate.","m":2,"cp":"abbasid-caliphate","cpn":"Abbasid Caliphate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","c":1},{"y":1275,"t":"contest_start","x":"1275: Bengal revolts.","cp":"Tughral Tughan Khan (Bengal)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban","c":3},{"y":1281,"t":"contest_end","x":"1281: Tughral is defeated and killed.","cp":"Tughral Tughan Khan (Bengal)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughral_Tughan_Khan","c":2},{"y":1285,"t":"contest_end","x":"9 March 1285: Prince Muhammad dies fighting the Mongols.","m":3,"cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban","c":2},{"y":1287,"t":"loss","x":"1287: Bengal under Bughra Khan.","m":1,"cp":"Bughra Khan's Bengal (Balbani rulers of Lakhnauti)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban","c":3},{"y":1290,"t":"dissolve","x":"1290: the Khalji Revolution ends the Mamluk dynasty.","m":6,"cp":"khalji-dynasty","cpn":"Khalji dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Iltutmish's war with Yildiz of Ghazni","from":1215,"to":1216,"outcome":"Iltutmish wins at Tarain on 25 January 1216; Yildiz is captured and later killed at Badaun.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish"},{"name":"Iltutmish's war with Qabacha of Multan","from":1217,"to":1228,"outcome":"Qabacha defeated: Uch falls on 4 May 1228, he drowns on 26 May; Multan and Uch under Iltutmish's governors.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish"},{"name":"Conquest of Bengal","from":1225,"to":1230,"outcome":"Tribute in 1225; Lakhnauti captured and Ghiyasuddin Iwaz executed in 1227; Balkha Khalji rebels in 1229 and is defeated in 1230.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish"},{"name":"Iltutmish's campaigns in Rajasthan and Malwa","from":1226,"to":1235,"outcome":"Ranthambore 1226, Mandore 1227, Gwalior 12 December 1232 captured; Bhilsa and Ujjain raided in 1234-1235 without annexation.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish"},{"name":"Mongol invasions of Punjab and Sindh","from":1221,"to":1285,"outcome":"Jalal ad-Din Mangburni defeated by Genghis Khan at the Indus in 1221 and flees to the Punjab (Iltutmish refuses him refuge); the Mongols raise a siege at Uch in 1246 (Balban) and sack Lahore in Bahram's reign (1240-1242); Prince Muhammad is killed on 9 March…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban"},{"name":"Bengal revolt of Tughral Tughan Khan","from":1275,"to":1281,"outcome":"Two Delhi armies fail; Balban invades Bengal himself in 1281 and kills Tughral; Bughra Khan is put in charge of Bengal and declares independence in 1287.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban"},{"name":"Khalji Revolution","from":1290,"to":1290,"outcome":"Jalal ud-Din Firuz Khalji ends the Mamluk dynasty (1 February to 13 June 1290); no territory changes hands.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate"}],"certainty":[{"from":1206,"to":1290,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty or survey frontier exists on the pages; the Punjab frontier with the Mongols, the Rajput marches and Bengal are approximate throughout."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mamluk_dynasty_(Delhi)","title":"Mamluk dynasty (Delhi)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qutb_ud-Din_Aibak","title":"Qutb ud-Din Aibak"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iltutmish","title":"Iltutmish"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delhi_Sultanate","title":"Delhi Sultanate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghiyas_ud_din_Balban","title":"Ghiyas ud din Balban"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narasingha_Deva_I","title":"Narasingha Deva I"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tughral_Tughan_Khan","title":"Tughral Tughan Khan"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_India","title":"Mongol invasions of India"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karnat_dynasty","title":"Karnat dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalachuris_of_Ratnapura","title":"Kalachuris of Ratnapura"}]}